        {
          "file": "src/billing/status.ts",
          "claim": "WHAT: Propagating NotReadyError from fetchStatus activates pollCharge's resubmit branch, which calls the non-idempotent gw.submit. WHY: errors.ts defines NotReadyError as 'the gateway has the charge but has not settled it yet', so resubmitting creates duplicate charges every time a charge is still pending settlement. HOW: In pollCharge, do not resubmit on NotReadyError; retry the status check or wait for the next tick, and only resubmit when the error semantics truly mean the charge was never received.",
          "keep": true,
          "rationale": "The finding identifies a real, distinct bug. errors.ts defines NotReadyError as 'The gateway has the charge but has not settled it yet (transient)', but poller.ts catches NotReadyError and calls gw.submit(charge.payload) to resend it, with a comment claiming NotReadyError means 'the gateway never received it'. Because the gateway already has the charge, resubmitting is unsafe and will duplicate charges. This is a consequence of the earlier change (propagating NotReadyError unchanged from fetchStatus), not the same problem the previous decision addressed. The prior decision only fixed fetchStatus converting retryable NotReadyError into terminal FailedError; it did not address pollCharge's misinterpretation of NotReadyError and its non-idempotent resubmit.",
